	Ø What is a File system?
	- It is a system used by an operation system to manage file. The system controls how data is saved or retrieved.
	- Operating system stores files and directories in an organized and structed way 
	- There are many different types of filesystems. In general, improvements have been made to filesystems with new releases of operating systems and each new file system has been given a different name 
		○ ext3, ext4, xfs - linux filesystems
		○ NTFS, FAT - windows filesystems

	Ø Navigating File System commands
	- $ cd  : Change directory (cd / )( cd .. -onestep back)(just cd takes to home directory
	- $ pwd : Print working directory (pwd )
	- $ ls : List (ls -ltr)
	

