	Ø File system structure and its Description
	- /boot	Contains file that is used by boot loader (grub.cfg)
	/root	root user home directory
	/dev 	System devices(eg disk, cdrom, speakers, flashdrive, keyboard, external peripherals) 
	/etc	Configuration files(sendmail, nfs, ….. Application on top of Linux os or comes with linux )
	/bin->/usr/bin	Everyday user command (ls, pwd,….)
	/sbin->/usr/sbin	System/filesystem commands ( filessystem, disks, extending filesystem….)
	/opt	Optional addon applications(Not part of OS apps) third party like oracle, sap etc
		
	/proc	Running processes(Only exist in Memory, ntg when turns off)
	/lib->/usr/lib	C programming library files needed by commands and apps
