	Ø Find files and directories 
	- Two main commands are used to find files/directories
		○ Find
			§ $ find from_location_to_search -name filename/directory
			§ $ find . -name "krammer" # .=pwd
		○ Locate
			§ $ locate krammer
	- If locate command does not output any result, then as root run "updatedb"
	- Also make sure you have "mlocate" package installed
		○ To check = rpm -qa | grep mlocate
		○ To install = yum install mlocate
	- Locate is fast 
	- find is hierarchical search
	Ø Difference between find and locate
	- Locate uses a prebuilt database, which should be regularly updated, while find iterates over a filesystem to locate files. Thus, locate is much faster than find, but can be inaccurate if the database (can be seen as a cache) is not updated. 

